course: dictionary
lesson: 14674
title: Prepared: ready and willing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Prepared has more than one meaning, so the words around it are your best clue. «I am prepared for the test» means I am ready for it, because I have studied and I know what to do.
explain: Prepared can also mean made ready earlier. «She read her prepared speech, which she had written the night before.» The clue is written the night before: the speech was ready before the day it was used.
explain: Prepared to means willing to do something. «I'm prepared to help you with your maths.» The clue is help: it shows you are ready and happy to do it. Prepared is also the past form of prepare, which means to get something ready.
fact: Prepared means ready for something.
fact: «Prepared» can mean made ready earlier, as in «a prepared speech».
fact: «Prepared to» means willing to do something: «I'm prepared to help.»
fact: «Prepared» is the past form of «prepare», which means to get something ready.
fact: «Be prepared» is a key safety idea: have a plan and a kit for emergencies.
exercise: «I am prepared for the test.» What does prepared mean here? | Surprised and shocked | Sent away from school | Tired after a long walk | *Ready for something
exercise: «I'm prepared to help you with your maths.» What does prepared to mean? | Lost in a crowd | *Willing to do something | Too busy to speak | Forced to stop
exercise: «She gave a prepared speech, written the night before.» Find and copy one word that tells you the speech was made ready earlier. | speech | *prepared | night | gave
test: «Mum prepared lunch before we got home.» What does prepared mean here? | *Got ready earlier | Threw it away | Forgot about it | Ate it all up
test: Which phrase means willing to do something? | *prepared to | prepared food | well prepared | come prepared
exam: The Scouts' motto is «Be Prepared». What does it mean? | Run away when things go wrong | Never leave the house | *Have a plan and a kit ready for emergencies | Wait for someone else to decide
